/-!
# Formation, resources and information in constraint multiset rewriting

The contextual guarded step uses the factored admission interface, with
equivalence to its original validity specification. Situated formation adds
scope inventories, authored locations and handle rights. Information includes
declared equality, constraint refinement and universal guard obligations.

The independent resource operator characterizes actual check-free schedules.
Contextual conditional certificates retain their original-prefix questions
and reconstruct existing executions at complete typed endpoints.

Persistent inference is connected through actual selected firings. Its
category modulo ordered proof observation is equivalent to supported source
proof contexts; its Cartesian maps retain premise occurrences. Requests
remain consumable, and arbitrary linear proof profiles are not identified
with this persistent profile.

Resource restriction preserves declared supported future observations,
including refusal. Native ownership, unrestricted minimization, arbitrary
schema installation and Flower profile refactoring are separate obligations.
-/
